    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "The power system operator issued an evidence-based grid status declaration for the Visayas island region, a response to a verified demand-supply imbalance. A generation equipment malfunction at Kepco SPC Power's Unit 2, combined with a documented cascade of generator failures since May, led to a measured generation shortfall of over 950 megawatts. This grid stabilization action was taken to mitigate heightened system vulnerability and elevated blackout probability.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Sage",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-0",
          "how-1",
          "how-2",
          "how-3",
